# script | mode | invocation | expects | notes
# Python-only owning-instance reader egregore_runtime/artifact_publication_cli.py is covered by tests/test_artifact_publication.py. This gate inventories shell readers only; the wrapper does not read or forward credentials.
bin/api-call.sh | covered | tests/test-api-call.sh | - | the dedicated suite runs all four credential hygiene classes
bin/artifacts.sh | probe | bash bin/artifacts.sh opens brief | exit=0 out=- | reads EGREGORE_API_KEY for the org-authenticated opens report of a hosted link; the key reaches curl on standard input, never in its arguments
bin/attendant.sh | exempt | - | - | 2026-09-23: daemon warmup and lifecycle need a bounded process fixture.
bin/codex-session-start.sh | exempt | - | - | 2026-09-23: startup fan-out needs isolated identity and Git fixtures.
bin/connector-arena.sh | exempt | - | - | 2026-10-07: the optional ARENA_TOKEN reaches the Python helper through the environment for pull and add and is sent by urllib as a bearer header, which the curl stub control plane cannot observe; bin/tests/test-connector-arena.sh checks that status never prints it and that add stops before any network without one.
bin/deploy-site.sh | exempt | - | - | 2026-09-23: deployment needs an isolated managed-site fixture.
